WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.789 --> 00:00:05.920
Shazam and Superman will appear on the silver
screen together in Spring 2019 - but it's

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.820
probably not the Man of Steel you know and
love.

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.900
Potential spoilers for Shazam! ahead!

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:16.270
We Got This Covered claims that sources in-the-know
say that Superman will appear in Shazam!,

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:19.369
the upcoming Zachary Levi-led DC superhero
flick.

00:00:19.369 --> 00:00:25.070
Shazam! tells the story of a 14-year-old orphan
named Billy Batson who meets a mystical wizard,

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:29.470
obtains the powers of six different immortal
elders, and earns the ability to turn into

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.540
an adult superhero whenever he utters the
word "Shazam!"

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.360
Are you for real?!"

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.000
"SAY IT!"

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.340
"Okay … Shazam?"

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:42.460
The movie looks like a cheery remedy to the
doomy, gloomy DC Extended Universe - but with

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.780
the Man of Steel reportedly making an appearance
in the movie, Shazam! will also feel like

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:50.180
it truly belongs in that Universe, for better
or for worse.

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:55.250
But before any DC enthusiasts start jumping
for joy or creating Shazam and Superman fan

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:59.690
art, we have some disappointing news: the
actor popping up in Shazam! may not be the

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:01.920
Superman star most people are familiar with.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:07.140
We Got This Covered claims, citing anonymous
insiders, that Henry Cavill won't be the man

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:09.380
playing the Metropolis Marvel in Shazam!

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:13.840
This is reportedly due to Cavill's disinterest
in returning to the role, which he first stepped

00:01:13.850 --> 00:01:16.290
into for 2013's Man of Steel.

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:20.780
The outlet further speculates that the, quote,
"ongoing alleged difficulties" between Warner

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.560
Bros. and DC Films executives and Cavill motivated
the decision.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:29.100
The Hollywood Reporter previously reported
that Cavill had allegedly cut ties with Warner

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.940
Bros. and was actively looking for a way out
of the DCEU and his role as Superman.

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:38.560
Batman star Ben Affleck was said to be doing
the same - leaving the studios without two

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.480
of their biggest superhero stars.

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.100
A Warner Bros. spokesperson, however, later
claimed,

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:47.300
"We have a great relationship and great respect
for Henry Cavill that continues to remain

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:48.140
unchanged.

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:52.900
Additionally we have made no current decisions
regarding any upcoming Superman films."

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:57.509
If Cavill is indeed out of the running, who
will portray Superman alongside Shazam?

00:01:57.509 --> 00:02:02.700
Well, word is that Shazam! is using a body
double of the same size and stature as Cavill

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:05.200
and not including the character's face in
the scene.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.020
How will that work?

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:10.520
Reportedly, the sequence in question sees
Billy fulfilling his foster brother Freddy's

00:02:10.539 --> 00:02:14.830
wish for Billy to appear as Shazam at their
school, proving that Freddy is friends with

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:16.200
a real-life superhero.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:21.260
Just after Shazam walks into the room, Superman
follows behind, officially making Freddy the

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.620
coolest kid in school.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:28.319
Cavill, for his part, has kept pretty quiet
about his relationship status with the DCEU.

00:02:28.319 --> 00:02:32.939
He only broke his silence by posting to Instagram
shortly after The Hollywood Reporter's story

00:02:32.939 --> 00:02:37.819
went live a bizarre video of himself wearing
a "Krypton Lifting Team" shirt and holding

00:02:37.819 --> 00:02:42.939
up an action figure of himself as Superman
while a dog-bark version of "The Blue Danube"

00:02:42.939 --> 00:02:44.109
played in the background.

00:02:44.109 --> 00:02:45.480
In other words: No comment.

00:02:45.969 --> 00:02:50.500
His manager, Dany Garcia, then went on the
record to state that, metaphorically speaking,

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.460
the Superman cape is still in Cavill's closet,
saying,

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:58.280
"[Warner Bros.] has been and continues to
be our partners as they evolve the DC Universe."

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:04.099
Fellow DCEU actor Jason Momoa, who made a
splash in his Aquaman solo movie in December,

00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:08.909
has also maintained that Cavill is "absolutely"
not done playing Superman and that he is definitely

00:03:08.909 --> 00:03:10.900
not leaving the DCEU.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:16.189
So perhaps Cavill is tied up trying to renegotiate
terms of a potential new contract with Warner

00:03:16.189 --> 00:03:20.799
Bros., or he's attempting to secure producing
credits and the ability to sign off on directors

00:03:20.799 --> 00:03:24.749
and writers for Superman films, as various
reports have suggested.

00:03:24.749 --> 00:03:28.889
He very well could be playing a waiting game,
standing firm and not stepping back into his

00:03:28.889 --> 00:03:31.340
Clark Kent role until his requests are met.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:36.780
Or maybe Cavill actually does appear in Shazam!,
in a hilarious cameo, and all these insider

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:38.919
reports are just a smokescreen?

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:42.720
It's no Deadpool, but Shazam! looks like it's
game to pull off such a stunt:

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:43.720
"Oh hey, what's up?

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:44.560
I'm a superhero."

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:49.260
We'll all found out the truth about Superman's
appearance in Shazam! when the film opens

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:50.760
in theaters on April 5th.

